{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC12actingTenantyy20FoundationEssentials4UUIDVSgKF","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","title":"actingTenant(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"actingTenant","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4UUIDV"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Act on a different tenant (or clear it), CONTRACT.md §5.2 rule 1, contract 1.51."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/actingTenant(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/actingtenant(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"actingTenant","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tenantID","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4UUIDV"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to clear: the next request sends no "},{"code":"X-Axiam-Tenant","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" header at all,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is what “the header is sent only when set” requires and what every client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that never calls this method already does.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gated on what this client knows, and nothing more"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (§5.2 rule 1’s own words)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A client holding a login result ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamUser"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"login"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verifyMfa"},{"type":"text","text":"\/OPAQUE\/an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MFA or WebAuthn setup completion) is refused client-side, with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"zero wire","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", unless that principal is "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamUser\/organizationLevel"},{"type":"text","text":" — an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant principal gets a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"403"},{"type":"text","text":" from the server for the same header change, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offering the switch anyway would turn a type-level distinction into a runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"failure the caller has to discover by trying. When"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamUser\/reachableTenantIDs"},{"type":"text","text":" narrows that reach (§5.2.3), a tenant outside it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is refused the same way (rule 4)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A client holding ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"text"